IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT domain

-- g3-nouns.l4: the nouns of Articles 8 to 10 (Part 4: the register, the restricted section, public access) that only group G3 uses,
-- and the one record of readings, `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10`, that every public decision of the group takes as an ordinary GIVEN.
-- Nouns only: no rule and no #EVAL lives here.  The shared nouns (Entity, Registered charity, Standing on the register, Kind of entity, Governor,
-- Required steps notice, Basis of deregistration, Decision of the Commissioner, Legal actor) are in domain.l4 and are not redeclared.
-- Every name added here carries the Article it belongs to, so that it is unique across the fleet.

§ `Part 4 -- Charity register (Articles 8 to 10): the nouns of group G3`

§§ `Article 8(2): the three sections of the register`

-- src:218 | (2) The register must be kept in such a way as to distinguish between –
-- src:219 | (a) the general section;
-- src:220 | (b) the restricted section; and
-- src:221 | (c) the historic section.
@ref Article 8(2) (src:218-221)
DECLARE `Section of the register` IS ONE OF
    `the general section`
    `the restricted section`
    `the historic section`

-- A dated entry of an entity in one section.  The section of the register an entity is in on a day is a function of its entries and of the day
-- (Article 8(2); see `Art 8(2) the section in which the entity is entered on`), not a stored flag; domain.l4's `Standing on the register` is the
-- stored form that the integrator checks against it.
DECLARE `Placement of an entity in a section of the register` HAS
    `the section` IS A `Section of the register`
    `date of the entry` IS A DATE

§§ `Article 8(3): the fourteen items entered in respect of a registered charity`

-- One constructor for each of the fourteen items.  The registered name and the registration number are entered under Article 12(2), not here.
-- src:222 | (3) The Commissioner must enter in the register, in respect of each registered charity (whether entered in the general or restricted section), in addition to the registered name and registration number entered under Article 12(2) –
-- src:223 | (a) a note of the status of the entity that is the registered charity, being –
-- src:224 | (i) the sub-paragraph of the definition “entity” in Article 2(1) within which the entity falls (including, in the case of an entity falling within one of sub-paragraphs (f) to (j) of that definition, whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)), and
-- src:225 | (ii) in the case of an entity falling within one of sub-paragraphs (e), (g), (h) or (j) of that definition, details of the enactment, Act of the States, Royal Charter, Act of the United Kingdom Parliament, Order in Council or foreign law, by virtue of which it falls within that sub-paragraph;
-- src:226 | (b) the names of each of the governors of the registered charity;
-- src:227 | (c) the principal address of the registered charity with the meaning of paragraph (4);
-- src:228 | (d) the address of any other premises in Jersey, other than a private dwelling house, at or from which the registered charity undertakes any activity;
-- src:229 | (e) a statement of the purposes of the registered charity (the charity’s “registered charitable purposes”), drawn by the charity from its constitution and approved by the Commissioner as accurately reflecting the constitution as to the purposes;
-- src:230 | (f) a statement (the charity’s “registered public benefit statement”), approved by the Commissioner, of the public benefit provided by the charity and of the means by which the charity ensures that it provides that public benefit;
-- src:231 | (g) the date on which the charity was registered;
-- src:232 | (h) if the registered charity is an organized religious charity, within the meaning of Article 28, a note of that fact and of the provision of the Order under that Article by virtue of which it is such a charity;
-- src:233 | (i) if the registered charity meets the charity test by virtue of an Order under Article 5(3), the text of the provision in the constitution that falls within paragraph (2) of that Article;
-- src:234 | (j) whether the registered charity has or has not sent its annual return for the most recent year;
-- src:235 | (k) if a required steps notice has been served on the registered charity, or on a governor of the registered charity, a note of that fact (or a copy of the notice) and of the date on which the notice was served;
-- src:236 | (l) if the registered name has been changed, the previous registered name or names;
-- src:237 | (m) if an Order under Article 13(9)(c) applies to the registered charity, any details or statement that must be entered on the register under that Order; and
-- src:238 | (n) any other information prescribed by the Minister by Order.
@ref Article 8(3)(a) to (n) (src:222-238)
DECLARE `Entry required by Article 8(3)` IS ONE OF
    `a note of the status of the entity`                                                                    -- (a)
    `the names of each of the governors`                                                                    -- (b)
    `the principal address`                                                                                 -- (c)
    `the address of any other premises in Jersey`                                                           -- (d)
    `the registered charitable purposes`                                                                    -- (e)
    `the registered public benefit statement`                                                               -- (f)
    `the date on which the charity was registered`                                                          -- (g)
    `a note that the charity is an organized religious charity`                                             -- (h)
    `the text of the provision in the constitution that falls within Article 5(2)`                          -- (i)
    `whether the charity has or has not sent its annual return for the most recent year`                    -- (j)
    `a note of a required steps notice and of the date on which it was served`                              -- (k)
    `the previous registered names`                                                                         -- (l)
    `the details or statement that must be entered under an Order under Article 13(9)(c)`                   -- (m)
    `other information prescribed by the Minister by Order`                                                 -- (n)

§§ `Article 8(3)(a): the note of the status of the entity`

-- What the note must say, computed from the kinds of entity (Article 2(1)) that G1 derives.
-- src:223 | (a) a note of the status of the entity that is the registered charity, being –
-- src:224 | (i) the sub-paragraph of the definition “entity” in Article 2(1) within which the entity falls (including, in the case of an entity falling within one of sub-paragraphs (f) to (j) of that definition, whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)), and
-- src:225 | (ii) in the case of an entity falling within one of sub-paragraphs (e), (g), (h) or (j) of that definition, details of the enactment, Act of the States, Royal Charter, Act of the United Kingdom Parliament, Order in Council or foreign law, by virtue of which it falls within that sub-paragraph;
@ref Article 8(3)(a) (src:223-225)
DECLARE `Requirement of the note of status (Article 8(3)(a))` HAS
    `sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) within which the entity falls` IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
    `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a)` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `sub-paragraphs for which details of the enactment or foreign law are required` IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`

-- What the register holds as the note of status.
DECLARE `Note of status recorded in the register (Article 8(3)(a))` HAS
    `sub-paragraphs of Article 2(1) recorded` IS A LIST OF `Kind of entity`
    `whether it also falls within sub-paragraph (a), as recorded` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `details of the enactment, Act of the States, Royal Charter, Act of the United Kingdom Parliament, Order in Council or foreign law` IS A MAYBE STRING

§§ `Article 8(3)(d) and 8(4): premises and the principal address`

-- src:228 | (d) the address of any other premises in Jersey, other than a private dwelling house, at or from which the registered charity undertakes any activity;
@ref Article 8(3)(d) (src:228)
DECLARE `Premises of a charity (Articles 8(3)(d) and 8(4))` HAS
    address IS A STRING
    `in Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN
    `a private dwelling house` IS A BOOLEAN
    `at or from which the charity undertakes an activity` IS A BOOLEAN

-- The facts the cascade of Article 8(4) reads.  Whether a Law requires a registered office or business address in Jersey is a fact about another enactment
-- (the Companies (Jersey) Law 1991, the Foundations (Jersey) Law 2009 and so on, which are not among the sources), so it is an input.
-- src:239 | (4) The principal address for the purpose of paragraph (3)(c) is –
-- src:240 | (a) if the registered charity is a company, foundation, or other entity required by its constitutional Law to have a registered office or business address in Jersey, the address of that registered office or that business address;
-- src:241 | (b) if the charity is not such an entity, the address of the main premises in Jersey at or from which the activities in Jersey of the registered charity are managed, controlled or undertaken, unless the premises are a private dwelling house; or
-- src:242 | (c) if neither sub-paragraph (a) nor (b) applies, the address in Jersey of one of the governors of the charity.
@ref Article 8(4) (src:239-242)
DECLARE `Facts for the principal address (Article 8(4))` HAS
    `its constitutional Law requires a registered office or business address in Jersey` IS A BOOLEAN
    `registered office or business address in Jersey` IS A MAYBE STRING
    `main premises in Jersey from which its activities in Jersey are managed, controlled or undertaken` IS A MAYBE `Premises of a charity (Articles 8(3)(d) and 8(4))`
    `addresses in Jersey of the governors` IS A LIST OF STRING

§§ `Article 8(3)(j): the annual return for the most recent year`

DECLARE `Annual return sent by a charity (Article 8(3)(j))` HAS
    `last day of the year to which it relates` IS A DATE
    `date sent` IS A DATE

-- src:234 | (j) whether the registered charity has or has not sent its annual return for the most recent year;
@ref Article 8(3)(j) (src:234)
DECLARE `Facts for the annual return entry (Article 8(3)(j))` HAS
    `a date on which the charity's financial year ends` IS A MAYBE DATE
    `annual returns sent` IS A LIST OF `Annual return sent by a charity (Article 8(3)(j))`

§§ `Article 8(3): the facts that decide which of the fourteen items are required`

DECLARE `Note of a required steps notice (Article 8(3)(k))` HAS
    `served on` IS A `Recipient of a required steps notice`
    `date served` IS A DATE
    `note or copy of the notice` IS A STRING

DECLARE `Facts for the items of Article 8(3)` HAS
    `other premises` IS A LIST OF `Premises of a charity (Articles 8(3)(d) and 8(4))`
    `principal address entered` IS A MAYBE STRING
    `previous registered names` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `information prescribed by an Order under Article 8(3)(n)` IS A LIST OF STRING

-- What the register holds for a registered charity, item by item, so that "which required items are missing" can be asked of it.
-- A MAYBE is NOTHING where the item has not been entered; a LIST is empty likewise.
DECLARE `Entry in the register for a registered charity (Article 8(3))` HAS
    `the registered charity` IS A `Registered charity`
    `note of status` IS A MAYBE `Note of status recorded in the register (Article 8(3)(a))`
    `names of the governors` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `principal address` IS A MAYBE STRING
    `addresses of other premises in Jersey` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `statement of purposes approved by the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `public benefit statement approved by the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `note of the organized religious charity and of the provision of the Order` IS A MAYBE STRING
    `text of the provision of the constitution within Article 5(2)` IS A MAYBE STRING
    `annual return sent for the most recent year` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
    `notes of required steps notices` IS A LIST OF `Note of a required steps notice (Article 8(3)(k))`
    `previous registered names` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `details or statement under an Order under Article 13(9)(c)` IS A MAYBE STRING
    `other information prescribed by Order` IS A LIST OF STRING

§§ `Article 8(5): the five items entered in the historic section`

-- src:243 | (5) The Commissioner must enter in the historic section, in relation to any formerly registered charity that has been deregistered –
-- src:244 | (a) the entity’s former registered number;
-- src:245 | (b) if the entity was registered in the general section, the name under which the entity was registered immediately before deregistration, and any names under which it was previously so registered;
-- src:246 | (c) a summary of the reason why the entity was deregistered, including, if that reason was a contravention of a required steps notice, the reason for the service of that notice;
-- src:247 | (d) the dates on which the entity was registered and deregistered; and
-- src:248 | (e) such other matters as the Minister may prescribe by Order.
@ref Article 8(5) (src:243-248)
DECLARE `Entry required by Article 8(5)` IS ONE OF
    `the entity's former registered number`                                          -- (a)
    `the name under which the entity was registered immediately before deregistration, and the names under which it was previously so registered`  -- (b)
    `a summary of the reason why the entity was deregistered`                        -- (c)
    `the dates on which the entity was registered and deregistered`                  -- (d)
    `such other matters as the Minister prescribes by Order`                         -- (e)

DECLARE `Facts for the items of Article 8(5)` HAS
    `placements of the entity before deregistration` IS A LIST OF `Placement of an entity in a section of the register`
    `previous registered names` IS A LIST OF STRING
    `matters prescribed by an Order under Article 8(5)(e)` IS A LIST OF STRING

§§ `Article 8(6): the documents retained for ten years`

-- src:249 | (6) The Commissioner must retain for 10 years, in respect of each registered charity, a copy of –
-- src:250 | (a) the constitution of the charity, and any amendments to it;
-- src:251 | (b) the annual returns of the charity;
-- src:252 | (c) any notice served on the charity under this Law; and
-- src:253 | (d) any other document prescribed by the Minister by Order.
@ref Article 8(6) (src:249-253)
DECLARE `Document of a kind within Article 8(6)` IS ONE OF
    `the constitution of the charity, or an amendment to it`                         -- (a)
    `an annual return of the charity`                                                -- (b)
    `a notice served on the charity under this Law`                                  -- (c)
    `a document prescribed by the Minister by Order`                                 -- (d)
    `a document of a kind that Article 8(6) does not list`

-- A copy the Commissioner holds.  The date it ceased to be operative is the date an amendment superseded it (the constitution), if any; a return or a notice is not superseded.
DECLARE `Copy held by the Commissioner (Article 8(6))` HAS
    kind IS A `Document of a kind within Article 8(6)`
    `date received or made` IS A DATE
    `date it ceased to be operative` IS A MAYBE DATE

DECLARE `Earliest day on which a copy may be discarded (Article 8(6))` IS ONE OF
    `the copy is not to be discarded while the charity remains registered`
    `the copy may be discarded on and after` HAS day IS A DATE
    `Article 8(6) does not require the copy to be retained`

§§ `Article 9(1): the public elements of the restricted section`

-- src:255 | (1) For the purpose of Article 10 the public elements of the restricted section are, in relation to each charity registered in that section –
-- src:256 | (a) the registration number (but not the registered name) of the charity;
-- src:257 | (b) the matters registered under sub-paragraphs (a), (e), (f), (j) and (k) of Article 8(3);
-- src:258 | (c) a summary, produced by the charity, to the satisfaction of the Commissioner, of the reasons for registration of the charity in the restricted section; and
-- src:259 | (d) any other element that may be prescribed by the Minister by Order.
@ref Article 9(1) (src:255-259)
DECLARE `Element of the restricted section (Article 9(1))` IS ONE OF
    `the registration number, but not the registered name`                           -- (a)
    `the note of status registered under Article 8(3)(a)`                            -- (b)
    `the registered charitable purposes registered under Article 8(3)(e)`            -- (b)
    `the registered public benefit statement registered under Article 8(3)(f)`       -- (b)
    `the note of the annual return registered under Article 8(3)(j)`                 -- (b)
    `the note of a required steps notice registered under Article 8(3)(k)`           -- (b)
    `a summary of the reasons for registration in the restricted section`            -- (c)
    `another element prescribed by the Minister by Order`                            -- (d)

-- Everything that can be entered in a section of the register, for the question whether it is in a public part (Article 10(3)).
DECLARE `Matter entered on the register` IS ONE OF
    `the registered name`
    `the registration number`
    `an item required by Article 8(3)` HAS item IS AN `Entry required by Article 8(3)`
    `the summary of the reasons for registration, produced by the charity`
    `an item required by Article 8(5)` HAS item IS AN `Entry required by Article 8(5)`
    `another element prescribed by an Order under Article 9(1)(d)`

DECLARE `Facts for the public elements (Article 9(1))` HAS
    `a summary of the reasons has been produced by the charity to the satisfaction of the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `an Order under Article 9(1)(d) prescribes another element` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Article 9(2) to (7): the request for entry in the restricted section`

-- src:273 | (5) A request under paragraph (2) must be accompanied by a statement of the applicant’s intention, in the event of refusal of the request, being –
-- src:274 | (a) in the case of an application for registration –
-- src:275 | (i) that that application should be treated as withdrawn, or
-- src:276 | (ii) that it should be treated as an application for entry in the general section of the register, on provision of any further information and evidence required for such an application; or
-- src:277 | (b) in the case of a charity registered in the general section of the register –
-- src:278 | (i) that the charity should remain so registered, or
-- src:279 | (ii) that the charity should be treated as applying to be deregistered, on provision of any further information and evidence required for such an application.
@ref Article 9(5) (src:273-279)
DECLARE `Intention stated with a request (Article 9(5))` IS ONE OF
    `that the application should be treated as withdrawn`                                                                                                        -- (a)(i)
    `that the application should be treated as an application for entry in the general section, on provision of any further information and evidence required`   -- (a)(ii)
    `that the charity should remain so registered`                                                                                                               -- (b)(i)
    `that the charity should be treated as applying to be deregistered, on provision of any further information and evidence required`                          -- (b)(ii)

DECLARE `Consequence of proceeding on the intention stated with a request (Article 9(7)(b))` IS ONE OF
    `the application is treated as withdrawn`
    `the application is treated as an application for entry in the general section, on provision of any further information and evidence required`
    `the charity remains registered in the general section`
    `the charity is treated as applying to be deregistered, on provision of any further information and evidence required`

-- The request itself, as Article 9(4) and (5) describe it.
DECLARE `Request for entry in the restricted section (Article 9)` HAS
    `made in the form published by the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `supported by information and evidence to the satisfaction of the Commissioner` IS A BOOLEAN
    `accompanied by a statement of the intention` IS A MAYBE `Intention stated with a request (Article 9(5))`

-- The Commissioner's three satisfactions of Article 9(6)(a) to (c): each is the Commissioner's state of mind, so each is an input.
DECLARE `Satisfaction of the Commissioner under Article 9(6)` HAS
    `satisfied that the request complied with paragraphs (4) and (5)` IS A BOOLEAN
    `satisfied that one of the conditions prescribed under paragraph (2) is met` IS A BOOLEAN
    `satisfied that there is no ground on which the request must be refused or, for a discretionary ground, should be refused` IS A BOOLEAN

-- src:263 | (3) The Order –
-- src:264 | (a) must prescribe grounds, that may include the exercise of discretion by the Commissioner, on which the Commissioner may accept or refuse such a request;
-- src:265 | (b) must specify, for the purpose of paragraph (2)(a) –
-- src:266 | (i) what constitutes soliciting,
-- src:267 | (ii) what constitutes a donation, and
-- src:268 | (iii) if the Order does not prescribe a description of persons, what constitutes the general public for the purpose of the Order; and
-- src:269 | (c) may make provision under sub-paragraph (b) by reference to the exercise of discretion by the Commissioner, or in any other manner.
@ref Article 9(3) (src:263-269)
DECLARE `Content of an Order under Article 9` HAS
    `prescribes grounds on which the Commissioner may accept or refuse a request` IS A BOOLEAN
    `specifies what constitutes soliciting` IS A BOOLEAN
    `specifies what constitutes a donation` IS A BOOLEAN
    `prescribes a description of persons` IS A BOOLEAN
    `specifies what constitutes the general public` IS A BOOLEAN

§§ `Article 10: public access`

-- src:289 | (2) The Minister may by Order provide for the Commissioner to make the public parts of the register available in any other specified manner, to the public or to such description of persons as may be specified, on payment of –
-- src:290 | (a) a specified charge; or
-- src:291 | (b) a charge determined and published by the Commissioner.
@ref Article 10(2) (src:289-291)
DECLARE `Charge for access to the public parts of the register (Article 10(2))` IS ONE OF
    `a specified charge`                                       -- (a)
    `a charge determined and published by the Commissioner`    -- (b)

DECLARE `Content of an Order under Article 10(2)` HAS
    `specifies another manner in which the public parts are made available` IS A BOOLEAN
    `payment required` IS A MAYBE `Charge for access to the public parts of the register (Article 10(2))`

§§ `The acts of Articles 8 to 10 and the matters an Order of the Minister prescribes`

-- What the Commissioner, the Minister or the court does in these Articles.  An act is typed by what is done (and by the matter it is done about),
-- not by the Article that mentions it; who does it is the PARTY of the rule (`Legal actor` in domain.l4).
DECLARE `Act in relation to the register` IS ONE OF
    `establish and maintain a register of charities`
    `keep the register so as to distinguish between the general, restricted and historic sections`
    `enter in the register an item required in respect of a registered charity` HAS item IS AN `Entry required by Article 8(3)`
    `enter in the historic section an item required in respect of a formerly registered charity` HAS item IS AN `Entry required by Article 8(5)`
    `discard a copy of a document`
    `make the public parts of the register available to the public on a website for inspection without charge`
    `enter a charity in the restricted section of the register`
    `give written notice of the refusal of a request`
    `proceed on the basis of the intention stated with the request` HAS intention IS AN `Intention stated with a request (Article 9(5))`
    `designate a matter as not being a public part of the register` HAS matter IS A `Matter entered on the register`
    `make an Order prescribing` HAS matter IS A `Matter that an Order of the Minister prescribes (Articles 8 to 10)`

-- The matters on which Articles 8 to 10 empower the Minister to make an Order.  The content of an Order is an input (BRIEF): none is among the sources.
-- Article 9(3)(a) and (b) say what the Order under Article 9(2) MUST contain; that is a limit on its content (`Content of an Order under Article 9`), not a further power.
DECLARE `Matter that an Order of the Minister prescribes (Articles 8 to 10)` IS ONE OF
    `other information to be entered in the register in respect of a registered charity`                       -- 8(3)(n)
    `other matters to be entered in the historic section`                                                      -- 8(5)(e)
    `other documents of which a copy is to be retained`                                                        -- 8(6)(d)
    `other elements of the restricted section that are public`                                                -- 9(1)(d)
    `the funding condition for entry in the restricted section`                                                -- 9(2)(a)
    `other conditions for entry in the restricted section`                                                     -- 9(2)(b)
    `another manner in which the public parts of the register are made available, on payment of a charge`      -- 10(2)

§§ `The readings: forks F3.1 to F3.13 (the R4 shape)`

-- One enumeration per fork point, one constructor per reading.  The FIRST constructor of each is the reading taken.  FRAGMENT-G3.md carries the register
-- (provision, the text that licenses each reading, why the one is taken, the discriminating case).

-- F3.1  Article 8(6): "retain for 10 years" says no starting point.  (The survey's third reading, a rolling window of copies received in the last ten years,
-- answers "may this copy be discarded" exactly as the first does, so it is not a reading; the third constructor here is the one that differs.)
DECLARE `When the ten years of retention under Article 8(6) begin` IS ONE OF
    `from the day the Commissioner receives or makes each copy`
    `from the day the charity is deregistered`
    `from the day the copy ceases to be operative`

-- F3.2  Article 8(3)(j): "the most recent year".  The enumeration is domain.l4's `Meaning of the year of an annual return` (IP33).

-- F3.3  Article 10(4): "in relation to a particular registered charity", where Article 1 excludes the historic section from "registered charity" and Article 10(3)(c) makes that section public.
DECLARE `Reach of Article 10(4) to an entity that has been deregistered` IS ONE OF
    `a registered charity is an entity entered in the general or the restricted section only`
    `a registered charity includes an entity formerly registered and entered in the historic section`

-- F3.4  Every period of years in these Articles ("10 years"): is the day of the event counted?
DECLARE `Whether the day of an event is counted in a period of years` IS ONE OF
    `the day of the event is not counted, so the last day of the period is the anniversary`
    `the day of the event is the first day, so the last day of the period is the day before the anniversary`

-- F3.5  Adding years to 29 February.
DECLARE `How a year is added to a date that does not exist in the target year` IS ONE OF
    `the date moves back to the last day of the month`
    `the date rolls forward into the next month`

-- F3.6  The day on which an entry in a section of the register takes effect (Article 8(3)(g), 8(5)(d): "the date on which" it was registered or deregistered).
DECLARE `The day on which an entry in a section of the register takes effect` IS ONE OF
    `on the day of the entry`
    `on the day after the entry`

-- F3.7  Article 8(3)(j): "the most recent year", asked on a given day.
DECLARE `Which year is the most recent year` IS ONE OF
    `the latest year that has ended before the day asked`
    `the year in progress on the day asked`

-- F3.8  Article 8(3)(k): "if a required steps notice has been served".
DECLARE `Which required steps notices Article 8(3)(k) notes` IS ONE OF
    `every notice that has been served`
    `only a notice that has not been complied with`

-- F3.9  Article 8(4)(a): "a company, foundation, or other entity required by its constitutional Law to have a registered office or business address in Jersey".
DECLARE `Which entities fall within Article 8(4)(a)` IS ONE OF
    `an entity that its constitutional Law requires to have a registered office or business address in Jersey`
    `every company and foundation, and any other entity that its constitutional Law so requires`

-- F3.10  Article 8(4)(b): "unless the premises are a private dwelling house", then Article 8(4)(c): "if neither sub-paragraph (a) nor (b) applies".
DECLARE `What follows when the main premises are a private dwelling house` IS ONE OF
    `Article 8(4)(b) does not apply, so Article 8(4)(c) is reached`
    `Article 8(4)(b) applies and gives no address`

-- F3.11  Article 8(5)(b): "if the entity was registered in the general section".
DECLARE `The section that decides Article 8(5)(b)` IS ONE OF
    `the section the entity was entered in immediately before deregistration`
    `any section the entity was ever entered in`

-- F3.12  Article 9(2)(a), (b): "the applicant meets", where the lead-in lets a registered charity request too.
DECLARE `Who must meet a condition prescribed under Article 9(2)` IS ONE OF
    `whoever makes the request, an applicant for registration or a registered charity`
    `only an applicant for registration`

-- F3.13  Article 8(3)(a): sub-paragraph (ba) of Article 2(1) was inserted from 16 October 2025 without amending Article 8(3)(a).
DECLARE `Whether Article 8(3)(a) reaches sub-paragraph (ba) of Article 2(1)` IS ONE OF
    `Article 8(3)(a) reaches only the sub-paragraphs it names`
    `Article 8(3)(a) treats sub-paragraph (ba) like sub-paragraphs (f) to (j) for the note of sub-paragraph (a) and like (e), (g), (h) and (j) for the details`

-- The record.  Each field is TYPICALLY the reading taken.
DECLARE `Interpretation of Articles 8 to 10` HAS
    `start of the ten years of retention` IS A `When the ten years of retention under Article 8(6) begin`
        TYPICALLY `from the day the Commissioner receives or makes each copy`
    `meaning of the year of an annual return` IS A `Meaning of the year of an annual return`
        TYPICALLY `the calendar year`
    `reach of Article 10(4)` IS A `Reach of Article 10(4) to an entity that has been deregistered`
        TYPICALLY `a registered charity is an entity entered in the general or the restricted section only`
    `counting the day of an event in a period of years` IS A `Whether the day of an event is counted in a period of years`
        TYPICALLY `the day of the event is not counted, so the last day of the period is the anniversary`
    `adding a year to a date that does not exist` IS A `How a year is added to a date that does not exist in the target year`
        TYPICALLY `the date moves back to the last day of the month`
    `day on which an entry takes effect` IS A `The day on which an entry in a section of the register takes effect`
        TYPICALLY `on the day of the entry`
    `the most recent year` IS A `Which year is the most recent year`
        TYPICALLY `the latest year that has ended before the day asked`
    `required steps notices noted` IS A `Which required steps notices Article 8(3)(k) notes`
        TYPICALLY `every notice that has been served`
    `entities within Article 8(4)(a)` IS A `Which entities fall within Article 8(4)(a)`
        TYPICALLY `an entity that its constitutional Law requires to have a registered office or business address in Jersey`
    `main premises that are a private dwelling house` IS A `What follows when the main premises are a private dwelling house`
        TYPICALLY `Article 8(4)(b) does not apply, so Article 8(4)(c) is reached`
    `section that decides Article 8(5)(b)` IS A `The section that decides Article 8(5)(b)`
        TYPICALLY `the section the entity was entered in immediately before deregistration`
    `who must meet a condition under Article 9(2)` IS A `Who must meet a condition prescribed under Article 9(2)`
        TYPICALLY `whoever makes the request, an applicant for registration or a registered charity`
    `reach of Article 8(3)(a) to sub-paragraph (ba)` IS A `Whether Article 8(3)(a) reaches sub-paragraph (ba) of Article 2(1)`
        TYPICALLY `Article 8(3)(a) reaches only the sub-paragraphs it names`
